Original novelrar code is MIT. No UnRAR, 7-Zip, or LZ4 implementation source is
vendored in this repository. Public-format specifications inform original
container parsers, codec experiments, and the RAR5 stored-file writer.

Implementation lanes (docs/LICENSING.md): STDLIB, CLEANROOM, HOST, OPTIONAL,
and REFUSED. These labels record provenance and project policy, not a legal
certification or a determination that unsupported operations are unlawful.

Optional runtime packages include py7zr (LGPL-2.1-or-later, plus dependency
terms) and cryptography (Apache-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause, plus dependency terms).
python-lz4 and an installed libarchive are independent test oracles.

Supplied-password ZIP/7z operations and the distinct NRX1 authenticated
password envelope are supported. RAR supplied-password AES decryption is implemented in-tree, including an original
OpenCL kernel. Compressed RAR decoding uses system libarchive or an explicitly
selected installed decoder. RAR compressed encoding and password search are not
implemented. See docs/RAR-ACCELERATION.md for exact bounds and test provenance.

See docs/RESEARCH_REPORT.md for tested scope, limitations, and sources.
